1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,140
In 1960, three scientists did the math,
1960年，三位科学家算了一笔账，

2
00:00:03,140 --> 00:00:06,980
and set the end of the world for November 13, 2026.
把世界末日定在了2026年11月13日。

3
00:00:06,980 --> 00:00:09,050
That's less than four weeks from today.
离今天不到四个星期。

4
00:00:09,050 --> 00:00:10,590
Friday the 13th, of course.
当然，还是个黑色星期五。

5
00:00:10,590 --> 00:00:11,960
It was published in Science,
论文发在《科学》杂志上，

6
00:00:11,960 --> 00:00:14,230
one of the most respected journals on Earth.
地球上最受尊敬的期刊之一。

7
00:00:14,230 --> 00:00:17,870
Today's question: why did a serious formula say we'd be squeezed to death?
今天的问题：一个正经公式，为什么说我们会被挤死？

8
00:00:17,870 --> 00:00:19,270
And why are we still here?
我们又为什么还在？

9
00:00:19,270 --> 00:00:21,360
Meet Mo. Mo is just one person.
认识一下小莫。小莫只是一个人。

10
00:00:21,360 --> 00:00:23,500
But Mo has a lot of relatives.
可小莫的亲戚，特别多。

11
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:27,480
Around 1800, there were about one billion people.
1800年前后，地球上大约十亿人。

12
00:00:27,480 --> 00:00:29,310
By 1927, two billion.
到1927年，二十亿。

13
00:00:29,310 --> 00:00:30,800
By 1974, four billion.
1974年，四十亿。

14
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:33,630
Each doubling came faster than the last.
每翻一倍，都比上一次更快。

15
00:00:33,630 --> 00:00:35,510
Normal fast growth is exponential:
普通的快速增长叫指数增长：

16
00:00:35,510 --> 00:00:37,890
double, double, double, at a steady pace.
按固定的节奏，翻倍，翻倍，再翻倍。

17
00:00:37,890 --> 00:00:40,230
Like a bank account with a fixed interest rate.
就像利率固定的存款。

18
00:00:40,230 --> 00:00:42,000
It gets huge, but never infinite.
会很大，但永远不会无穷大。

19
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,720
Twist one: the team thought humans grow even faster than exponential.
反转一：他们认为，人类比指数增长还快。

20
00:00:45,720 --> 00:00:48,350
More people means more ideas and more teamwork,
人越多，点子越多，合作越多，

21
00:00:48,350 --> 00:00:50,660
and more ideas mean even faster growth.
点子越多，增长就越快。

22
00:00:50,660 --> 00:00:52,690
So the growth rate itself keeps growing.
增长的速度本身也在增长。

23
00:00:52,690 --> 00:00:54,990
Mathematicians call this hyperbolic growth.
数学家管这叫双曲增长。

24
00:00:54,990 --> 00:00:58,180
Their formula: population equals a big number,
他们的公式：人口等于一个大数，

25
00:00:58,180 --> 00:01:00,860
divided by the years left until 2026.
除以离2026年还剩多少年。

26
00:01:00,860 --> 00:01:02,930
Divide by a smaller and smaller number,
除数越来越小，

27
00:01:02,930 --> 00:01:05,110
and the answer rockets toward infinity.
答案就冲向无穷大。

28
00:01:05,110 --> 00:01:08,430
That's a singularity: a definite date with an infinite answer.
这叫奇点：一个确定的日子，一个无穷大的答案。

29
00:01:08,430 --> 00:01:11,470
The scary part? It fit two thousand years of data,
吓人的是：它拟合了两千年的数据，

30
00:01:11,470 --> 00:01:13,600
24 estimates of world population.
一共24个世界人口估计值。

31
00:01:13,600 --> 00:01:15,560
1800, 1927, 1974:
1800年，1927年，1974年，

32
00:01:15,560 --> 00:01:20,070
it came surprisingly close every time.
它都算得八九不离十。

33
00:01:20,070 --> 00:01:22,200
Experts wrote in calling it ridiculous.
专家写信说它荒唐。

34
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:23,620
The authors fought back.
作者照样据理力争。

35
00:01:23,620 --> 00:01:26,310
Twist two: plug today's date into the formula,
反转二：把今天的日期代进公式，

36
00:01:26,310 --> 00:01:29,220
and Earth should hold about 2.5 trillion people.
地球上应该有大约两万五千亿人。

37
00:01:29,220 --> 00:01:30,620
That's three hundred people
相当于每个真人身边，

38
00:01:30,620 --> 00:01:32,390
for every person actually alive.
再挤上三百个。

39
00:01:32,390 --> 00:01:34,950
The real number? About 8.3 billion.
真实的数字呢？大约八十三亿。

40
00:01:34,950 --> 00:01:36,480
So what bent the curve?
是什么把曲线掰弯了？

41
00:01:36,480 --> 00:01:37,940
Not famine. Not war.
不是饥荒，也不是战争。

42
00:01:37,940 --> 00:01:41,160
Right around the early 1960s, the growth rate peaked,
就在1960年代初，人口增长率到顶，

43
00:01:41,160 --> 00:01:42,790
and then started falling.
然后开始往下走。

44
00:01:42,790 --> 00:01:44,050
Kids stopped dying young.
孩子不再早早夭折。

45
00:01:44,050 --> 00:01:47,090
And when most kids survive, families choose to have fewer.
大多数孩子能长大，家庭就选择少生。

46
00:01:47,090 --> 00:01:48,890
Today the global birth rate
今天全球的出生率，

47
00:01:48,890 --> 00:01:51,750
is less than half of what it was in 1960.
还不到1960年的一半。

48
00:01:51,750 --> 00:01:53,780
Twist three: the authors had a prescription:
反转三：作者当年开过一个药方：

49
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:55,150
cut the birth rate in half.
把出生率砍掉一半。

50
00:01:55,150 --> 00:01:56,420
The world roughly did it.
世界差不多真做到了。

51
00:01:56,420 --> 00:01:58,570
In a way, the prophecy cancelled itself.
某种意义上，预言把自己给破了。

52
00:01:58,570 --> 00:02:00,150
When a formula hits infinity,
公式里一出现无穷大，

53
00:02:00,150 --> 00:02:03,420
it usually means the model has stopped describing reality.
通常说明模型已经不再描述现实。

54
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:05,080
Like a balloon you keep blowing up:
就像一直吹的气球：

55
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:07,190
the math says forever, the rubber says no.
数学说能无限大，橡皮说不行。

56
00:02:07,190 --> 00:02:09,330
Fun fact: the lead author, von Foerster,
冷知识：第一作者冯·福斯特，

57
00:02:09,330 --> 00:02:10,830
was once a stage magician.
还当过舞台魔术师。

58
00:02:10,830 --> 00:02:13,420
One historian called the paper a magic trick:
一位历史学家说，这篇论文就是个魔术：

59
00:02:13,420 --> 00:02:15,560
ordinary math, extraordinary title.
普通的内容，惊人的标题。

60
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:18,860
And the trick worked: Time magazine and the New York Times covered it.
魔术成功了：《时代》周刊和《纽约时报》都报道了它。

61
00:02:18,860 --> 00:02:21,990
Friendly fine print: the formula was never a real forecast.
友情提示：这个公式从来不是真预言，

62
00:02:21,990 --> 00:02:23,750
It was a warning about a curve.
它是一个关于曲线的警告。

63
00:02:23,750 --> 00:02:25,700
Today population growth is slowing,
如今人口增长在放慢，

64
00:02:25,700 --> 00:02:28,590
and many countries now worry about too few babies.
不少国家反倒发愁孩子太少。

65
00:02:28,590 --> 00:02:30,950
So on November 13, relax. Mo is fine.
所以11月13号，放轻松，小莫没事。

66
00:02:30,950 --> 00:02:34,170
Maybe just don't schedule anything important.
不过那天，重要的事还是别排了。

